#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010| title=Born Confused|author=Tanuja Desai Hidier | page=| passage=I caught sight of something that seemed the nexus of all that glittered, all that '''golded''': like a hallucination in the traffic's rotary heart, a saried creature giddily swirling her own razored rainbow roundabout, mirrored fabric sending light spinning like saberlike amidst the smoking, choking cars.}}
